alse},{"lineNumber":26,"author":{"gitId":"-"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2019-07-29T17:14:46","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":27,"author":{"gitId":"-"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2021-07-17T16:49:07","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":28,"author":{"gitId":"-"},"content":"## Feature XYZ","lastModifiedDate":"2024-01-07T18:33:52","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":29,"author":{"gitId":"-"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2024-01-07T18:33:52","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":30,"author":{"gitId":"-"},"content":"// Feature details","lastModifiedDate":"2024-01-07T18:33:52","isFullCredit":false}],"authorContributionMap":{"Kytersaurus":1,"-":29}},{"path":"seedu-git-standard/SKILL.md","fileType":"md","lines":[{"lineNumber":1,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"---","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":2,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"name: seedu-git-standard","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":3,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"description: Apply the SE-EDU Git conventions to commits and branches in this project.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":4,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"---","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":5,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":6,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"# SE-EDU Git standard","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":7,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":8,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"Use this skill whenever creating, reviewing, or proposing a commit or branch in this project. Follow https://se-education.org/guides/conventions/git.html.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":9,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":10,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"## Commits","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":11,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":12,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"- Write a meaningful subject in imperative mood, capitalize its first letter, omit the final period, and keep it under 50 characters when practical (72 characters maximum).","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":13,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"- Add a body for non-trivial commits. Separate it from the subject with a blank line, wrap it at 72 characters, and use blank lines between paragraphs.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":14,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"- Explain what changed and why it changed, using present tense for the situation and imperative mood for the change. Do not explain implementation details that the diff already shows.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":15,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"- Use a scope or category prefix only when it improves clarity.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":16,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":17,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"## Branches","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":18,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":19,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"- Use meaningful kebab-case names.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":20,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"- For issue-related branches, use `\u003cissue-number\u003e-\u003ckeywords-from-issue-title\u003e`.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false}],"authorContributionMap":{"Kytersaurus":20}},{"path":"seedu-java-coding-standard/SKILL.md","fileType":"md","lines":[{"lineNumber":1,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"---","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":2,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"name: seedu-java-coding-standard","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":3,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"description: Apply the SE-EDU basic and intermediate Java coding standard to Java code in this project.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":4,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"---","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":5,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":6,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"# SE-EDU Java coding standard","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":7,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":8,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"Use this skill for all Java code in this project. Follow https://se-education.org/guides/conventions/java/intermediate.html and use Google Java Style for uncovered topics.","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":9,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"","lastModifiedDate":"2026-08-28T17:18:40","isFullCredit":false},{"lineNumber":10,"author":{"gitId":"Kytersaurus"},"content":"- Put every class in a lower-case project package; use PascalCase nouns for classes, camelCase verbs